WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.320
- We're traveling to Kyiv

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.519
from Lviv where we've been
for the past two months.

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:10.269
(dramatic music)

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.530
It's still kind of dangerous to go back

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.650
but we really wanted to go back home

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.050
to check on our apartment, the parents,

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.713
so we're going back.

00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:34.463
(dramatic music)

00:00:51.724 --> 00:00:53.150
The roads to Kyiv have been perfect.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.580
Like this specific highway
we're on, it is Kyiv-Chop,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.976
which goes all the way to western Ukraine.

00:00:57.976 --> 00:01:00.726
(dramatic music)

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.150
Traveling to Kyiv is about
seven to eight hours.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.910
The biggest issue is getting gas.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.450
So we are at a gas station right now.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.100
Not a lot of them have any kind of gas.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.960
A lot of them have limitations

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.240
in how much you can get into one car.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.763
So we have to visit quite
a few of them on the way.

00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:38.830
(dramatic music)

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.210
All the signs and all the guidance

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.620
and directions across the
roads have been removed.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.398
Once the war started, we
have gotten information

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:49.700
and guidance from our
government in many ways,

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.650
and one of the ways

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.610
has been for the people
to remove the signs

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.210
and basically any names of cities

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.670
and villages that are on
the road as you travel.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.440
So if and when Russian occupants make it

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.170
to this specific region,

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.000
it's very hard for them to orient,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.560
even for us when we're
traveling back home,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.200
we really have to go with the map

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.200
because there are no
pointers on where to travel.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.649
And you really have to know
the road to get back home.

00:02:16.649 --> 00:02:18.710
(dramatic music)

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:20.870
So we're in Kyiv region right now.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.080
Probably around 10 to 15 miles from Kyiv.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.030
There's a lot of destruction here,

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.223
a lot of residential homes,

00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:29.490
a lot of infrastructure.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.960
The bridge over the road,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.020
this has been a way to cross the highway

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.750
has been entirely removed

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.320
by our governmental officials and the army

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.590
so the occupants' job would
be harder to get to places

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.570
and to settle here for
a longer period of time.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.103
We saw multiple bridges like this.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.030
Even though the cities around Kyiv

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.870
and the region and the villages

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.440
have taken a lot of heavy
fighting and destruction,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.640
everything has been removed apart

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.840
from just a few pieces of
like tanks or machinery

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.043
just for people to see the
destroyed Russian vehicles.

00:03:10.134 --> 00:03:15.134
(pensive music)
(camera clicking)

00:03:25.464 --> 00:03:30.464
(voices murmuring)
(pensive music)

